    given-names: "Jan"
    affiliation: "Vision for Robotics and Autonomous Systems, Czech Technical University in Prague"
    email: "vlkjan6@fel.cvut.cz"
title: "map_data: OSM-based map processing and path planning for outdoor robot navigation"
version: 1.3.0
date-released: 2026-08-24
license: BSD-3-Clause
url: "https://vras-robotour.github.io/map_data/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vras-robotour/map_data"
abstract: >-
  A ROS2 package and standalone Python library that parses GPX waypoints,
  downloads and classifies OpenStreetMap features into traversable footways,
  roads, and barriers, and plans cost-aware paths using graph A*, grid A*, and
  RRT*. It includes an interactive web viewer for inspecting and annotating map
  data, and a ROS2 node that publishes a cost-aware footway point cloud for
  outdoor robot navigation.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - ROS2
  - OpenStreetMap
  - path planning
  - autonomous navigation
  - RRT*
